{:fh/id  "FH-CTRL-001"
 :fh/law "A controller record is keyed by the controller kind plus the caller-supplied :control address, so two occurrences of one view given DIFFERENT addresses hold independent records: an edit at one occurrence moves only its own record, and the other keeps showing its baseline."

 ;; The library's controller family. The KIND is the library's — which
 ;; protocol this record obeys — and it is half of every record key.
 :kind    :my.ui/buffered-field

 ;; Two occurrences of ONE view, mounted side by side, each given the
 ;; domain identity that owns its state. Nothing here is derived from
 ;; render position: these are the addresses the CALL SITES pass.
 :control-a [:invoice 1 :amount]
 :control-b [:invoice 2 :amount]

 ;; The external baseline each occurrence shows while it holds no record.
 :value-a "100.00"
 :value-b "250.00"

 ;; One edit, at occurrence A only.
 :typed "12."

 ;; What the two occurrences display afterwards: A shows its draft, B is
 ;; untouched. Independence is the whole claim.
 :displayed-after-edit ["12." "250.00"]

 ;; And the record table holds exactly ONE record — A's — under the pair
 ;; key. B never acquired one, because nothing wrote to B.
 :record-keys-after-edit [[:my.ui/buffered-field [:invoice 1 :amount]]]}
